technical_body = f'''<nav class="nav"><a class="brand" href="index.html">← BELIEFWEAVE</a><div class="navlinks"><a href="paper.pdf">Paper</a><a href="benchmark.html">Benchmark</a></div></nav><section class="hero" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;border-top:0;padding-bottom:20px"><div><div class="eyebrow">Technical deep dive</div><h1 style="font-size:72px">Inside BeliefWeave.</h1><p>The pieces I added to make memory updates traceable and to keep uncertain memories from silently changing behavior.</p></div></section><section><h2>Core components</h2><div class="cards"><div class="card"><h3>Typed temporal memory</h3><p>Content, type, source events, source type, confidence, validity, status, scope, supersession, conflict links, and user verification.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Structural safety gates</h3><p>Learned conflict decisions are bounded by compatible memory types and entity-aware semantics before destructive state updates are allowed.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Decision-aware authority</h3><p>Retrieved beliefs are separately scored for permission to influence behavior, enabling USE / ASK / ABSTAIN.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Training / learned components</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Artifact size</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Observation router</td><td>~212 KB</td><td>Routes candidate user information into memory-relevant classes.</td></tr><tr><td>Conflict classifier</td><td>~67 KB</td><td>Assists compatible update/conflict decisions behind structural gates.</td></tr><tr><td>Write policy</td><td>~6 KB</td><td>Baseline learned policy for persist / temporary / ask / ignore decisions.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="fine">I kept these components small so the full path can be run locally. They are not meant to stand in for a frontier model.</p></section><section><h2>Evaluation methodology</h2><div class="cards"><div class="card"><h3>Temporal</h3><p>Preference reversal, expiry, contradiction and state-retirement probes.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Retrieval</h3><p>Hit@1, Hit@3, MRR, context sensitivity, and stale-memory leak checks.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Authority</h3><p>CPR, false personalization, use precision, intervention fidelity, ASK/ABSTAIN behavior.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Reliability</h3><p>Calibration, OOD paraphrases, randomized invariants, an exhaustive 9,600-state authority-policy audit, database integrity, privacy erasure, concurrency stress, and the API contract.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Source artifacts</h2><div class="artifactGrid"><a class="artifact" href="downloads/TECHNICAL_REPORT.md"><small>Report</small><b>Technical report</b><span>Full engineering write-up.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/beliefweave-code.zip"><small>Code</small><b>Reproducibility bundle</b><span>Core, tests, scripts, benchmarks.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/{wheel.name}"><small>Wheel</small><b>Installable package</b><span>BeliefWeave Python distribution.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="README.md"><small>Guide</small><b>Repository README</b><span>Quickstart and artifact map.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md"><small>Design</small><b>Architecture decisions</b><span>Tradeoffs behind authority, reproducibility, deletion, and storage scope.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/authority_modelcheck.json"><small>Assurance</small><b>Authority model check</b><span>Finite exhaustive declared-state verification for V1/V2/V3.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/privacy_erasure.json"><small>Privacy</small><b>Erasure regression</b><span>Provenance-safe hard-forget and export leakage checks.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/privacy_inventory.json"><small>Privacy</small><b>User data inventory</b><span>Complete export inventory, full erasure, guarded replay tombstones, and keyed telemetry identifiers.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/database_resilience.json"><small>Reliability</small><b>Process resilience</b><span>Independent-process writes and interpreter-crash rollback on the SQLite reference runtime.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/atomicity_fault_injection.json"><small>Transactionality</small><b>Atomic ingest fault injection</b><span>Injected crashes after memory insertion and during conflict resolution leave no partial writes.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/experiment_lineage.json"><small>Reproducibility</small><b>Experiment lineage</b><span>SHA256-linked code, inputs, commands, and result artifacts.</span></a><a class="artifact" href="downloads/core_install.json"><small>Packaging</small><b>Dependency-free core install</b><span>Clean-venv wheel smoke test with no optional ML dependencies installed.</span></a></div></section>'''
(SITE / "technical.html").write_text(page("BeliefWeave — Technical Deep Dive", technical_body))

